---
description: Behavioral constraints for Vibe Prospecting workflows - lazy evaluation, never auto-export, user-facing simplicity, autocomplete for required filters, standardized presentation.
alwaysApply: true
---

prospecting-workflow:

- Lazy evaluation: Show sample data (up to 5 rows) immediately. Full dataset processes only on explicit export.
- Never auto-export. Always show cost and wait for explicit user confirmation before calling export-to-csv.
- User-facing: Say  "Vibe Prospecting" in responses. Never expose session_id, table_name, or internal tool names.
- For filters linkedin_category, naics_category, job_title, business_intent_topics, company_tech_stack_tech, city_region: always call autocomplete first and use the returned standardized values in fetch-entities.
- Present results in standardized markdown table format with cost_in_credits. Use left-join style with all available fields.
- Never expose internal table names or technical internals to the user.
- Use one comprehensive fetch-entities call when filters can be combined; avoid multiple fetch calls.
- For event previews, state that the sample shows up to 3 events per entity and that export returns the full dataset.